.TH DUP2 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
dup2 \- duplicate a file descriptor to a specified number
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int dup2(int " descriptor ", int " new_descriptor ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Duplicates an open descriptor onto
.IR new_descriptor .
If the destination is already open, Linux closes and replaces it atomically.
The two descriptors share an open file description. If both arguments are
equal and the descriptor is valid, the call does nothing and succeeds.
Otherwise the new descriptor does not have close\-on\-exec set.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the destination descriptor, or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.BR <errno.h> .
Errors include
.BR EBADF ,
.BR EBUSY ,
and
.BR EINTR .
Other Linux dup2 errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dup (3crunch),
.BR close (3crunch),
.BR dup2 (2)
